  "_about": [
    "Spiritpedia's emotional-search safety data: the crisis intercept, the dual path, the soft tier, the medical disclaimer, and the phrase lists the search uses to understand what people type.",
    "ONE FILE FOR BOTH. The website (web/utils/emotionSearchPatterns.js) and the app (app/lib/core/safety/) both read this file, so they can never drift. Edit it here and both change.",
    "Changing it redeploys the website. Run `npm test` in web/ and `flutter test` in app/ first: both check web/shared/emotion-safety.cases.json, which pins the expected behaviour.",
    "Why each list is the way it is — which phrases were added when, and why some are multi-word — is explained in the comments in web/utils/emotionSearchPatterns.js.",
    "All phrases are lower-case and apostrophe-free: matching happens after normalisation."
